1
00:00:08,092 --> 00:00:08,968
<i>Night.</i>

2
00:00:09,552 --> 00:00:11,429
<i>A time of mystery.</i>

3
00:00:12,304 --> 00:00:15,181
<i>All living creatures drift off to sleep</i>

4
00:00:15,182 --> 00:00:17,518
<i>and are drawn into the world of dreams.</i>

5
00:00:18,185 --> 00:00:20,730
<i>There, they find respite.</i>

6
00:00:22,022 --> 00:00:26,318
<i>One man held sway over that healing power.</i>

7
00:00:27,194 --> 00:00:31,240
<i>But one day, he suddenly vanished.</i>

8
00:00:32,408 --> 00:00:36,035
<i>Night lost its power,
and the world of dreams</i>

9
00:00:36,036 --> 00:00:38,581
<i>became nothing more than a dream.</i>

10
00:00:39,999 --> 00:00:43,627
<i>Peace on earth was lost as well.</i>

11
00:00:44,712 --> 00:00:47,589
<i>As everyone prayed for the man's return,</i>

12
00:00:47,590 --> 00:00:50,384
<i>someone eventually appeared before them.</i>

13
00:00:51,969 --> 00:00:53,845
<i>Would he bring them</i>

14
00:00:53,846 --> 00:00:56,055
<i>the peace they had once known?</i>

15
00:00:56,056 --> 00:00:57,641
<i>Or...</i>

16
00:02:42,997 --> 00:02:44,956
Everyone, get away from here!

17
00:02:44,957 --> 00:02:46,584
Insomniac!

18
00:03:01,807 --> 00:03:03,142
What the hell was that?

19
00:03:04,727 --> 00:03:08,647
MY NAME'S NOT INSOMNIAC FOR NOTHING

20
00:03:10,566 --> 00:03:12,985
<i>The mysterious boy's attack</i>

21
00:03:13,569 --> 00:03:17,656
<i>left the castle
in the Country of Long Nights in ruins.</i>

22
00:03:34,048 --> 00:03:35,341
Insomniac...

23
00:03:36,926 --> 00:03:39,218
<i>But in my eyes,
what I've been saddled with</i>

24
00:03:39,219 --> 00:03:42,222
<i>is the castellan's job
and the land, not you.</i>

25
00:03:44,975 --> 00:03:47,561
Ice, fire, and steel...

26
00:03:48,854 --> 00:03:50,355
I see.

27
00:03:50,356 --> 00:03:54,525
So you're the reason those powers
seemed so scattered.

28
00:03:54,526 --> 00:03:58,489
Why are you cloaked in so many blessings?

29
00:03:59,239 --> 00:04:01,032
Who are you?

30
00:04:01,033 --> 00:04:03,326
Why is your hair black?

31
00:04:03,327 --> 00:04:08,123
That powerful red isn't from here
or the Country of Cold, is it?

32
00:04:09,166 --> 00:04:11,669
Answer my questions first.

33
00:04:12,753 --> 00:04:16,757
Why did you destroy the building
Insomniac was in?

34
00:04:18,217 --> 00:04:20,843
He was right there! Didn't you see him?

35
00:04:20,844 --> 00:04:23,805
Oh, you mean Night?

36
00:04:23,806 --> 00:04:27,226
Well, I thought I'd pin him
under the rubble and capture him.

37
00:04:27,977 --> 00:04:32,189
Night isn't human,
so that wouldn't kill him, would it?

38
00:04:34,608 --> 00:04:37,318
It bunches up around my elbows
when I wear it underneath,

39
00:04:37,319 --> 00:04:40,071
so I prefer draping it
over my shoulders like this.

40
00:04:40,072 --> 00:04:41,614
I'll pass on the sweets.

41
00:04:41,615 --> 00:04:43,367
You and Johann can have them.

42
00:04:43,951 --> 00:04:47,121
Chilly's caught another cold.

43
00:04:50,499 --> 00:04:53,544
Walpurga will be here soon.

44
00:04:54,044 --> 00:04:55,421
I have to get Night before...

45
00:04:59,800 --> 00:05:03,721
Don't talk like you know
a damn thing about him!

46
00:05:10,060 --> 00:05:11,145
Kastehelmi...

47
00:05:11,895 --> 00:05:13,272
Kastehelmi...

48
00:05:13,981 --> 00:05:15,399
Kastehelmi!

49
00:05:25,367 --> 00:05:28,996
The enemy's attack destroyed
the second-floor passage on the east side.

50
00:05:29,496 --> 00:05:33,082
Marronnier's knight commander
and his aide were caught in the attack

51
00:05:33,083 --> 00:05:35,502
and appear to have fallen.
Their condition is unknown.

52
00:05:36,211 --> 00:05:40,132
We'll immediately carry out the captain's
order to launch an all-out attack.

53
00:05:48,932 --> 00:05:50,433
That hurt...

54
00:05:50,434 --> 00:05:53,020
You're a nuisance.

55
00:06:00,569 --> 00:06:02,695
Please don't be so reckless.

56
00:06:02,696 --> 00:06:05,115
You're our honored guest.

57
00:06:05,699 --> 00:06:07,575
An honored guest

58
00:06:07,576 --> 00:06:10,536
you didn't bother evacuating
with the diplomat.

59
00:06:10,537 --> 00:06:12,288
My apologies.

60
00:06:12,289 --> 00:06:17,336
But I thought it unseemly to urge another
nation's knight commander to retreat.

61
00:06:20,506 --> 00:06:22,508
I have to find Night right away.

62
00:06:23,509 --> 00:06:24,468
Whoa there.

63
00:06:27,513 --> 00:06:29,890
Don't falter now! Fire!

64
00:06:31,725 --> 00:06:32,768
Bang!

65
00:06:38,023 --> 00:06:42,735
The blessing of ice is here.
I hardly have to use my own power.

66
00:06:42,736 --> 00:06:44,487
He's a damn monster.

67
00:06:44,488 --> 00:06:48,032
You're rather different
from my first impression of you, Eleonora.

68
00:06:48,033 --> 00:06:52,453
Never mind that, Captain.
He's not that strong up close.

69
00:06:52,454 --> 00:06:53,996
True.

70
00:06:53,997 --> 00:06:56,082
But how do we get him into close combat?

71
00:06:56,083 --> 00:06:57,584
I doubt he'll let us get close.

72
00:07:02,673 --> 00:07:04,049
Damn it!

73
00:07:05,801 --> 00:07:07,261
What in the world is going on?

74
00:07:09,138 --> 00:07:11,097
What a terrible mess.

75
00:07:11,098 --> 00:07:12,141
Lady Kastehelmi!

76
00:07:12,808 --> 00:07:13,934
Why are you here?

77
00:07:14,434 --> 00:07:16,602
The hearth spirit called me.

78
00:07:16,603 --> 00:07:18,605
It must have sensed something was wrong.

79
00:07:19,231 --> 00:07:23,526
So, even the hearths
in this country have spirits?

80
00:07:23,527 --> 00:07:27,321
Are you all right, Johann? Are you hurt?

81
00:07:27,322 --> 00:07:31,159
I'm fine. Strangely enough,
I don't have a scratch.

82
00:07:31,160 --> 00:07:35,705
That red must be protecting you
from the evil spirits of other lands.

83
00:07:35,706 --> 00:07:36,540
Red?

84
00:07:40,294 --> 00:07:42,379
Then you should take this.

85
00:07:43,172 --> 00:07:44,965
The intruder is still up there.

86
00:07:47,176 --> 00:07:49,052
I need to dig Insomniac out.

87
00:07:50,095 --> 00:07:51,388
I'm certain he is unharmed.

88
00:07:56,185 --> 00:07:58,353
It's dangerous here.
You should stand back.

89
00:07:59,229 --> 00:08:00,314
All right.

90
00:08:01,523 --> 00:08:03,858
Insomniac! Where are you? Answer me!

91
00:08:03,859 --> 00:08:06,486
Huh? Wait! Night is my...

92
00:08:08,655 --> 00:08:11,074
Insomniac is your what?

93
00:08:16,246 --> 00:08:17,663
I can't sense him.

94
00:08:17,664 --> 00:08:18,916
Is he not here?

95
00:08:19,583 --> 00:08:20,918
No, he must be...

96
00:08:31,470 --> 00:08:33,764
Lady Kastehelmi, get back inside! Hurry!

97
00:08:34,348 --> 00:08:36,725
The bastard can control beasts too?

98
00:08:44,942 --> 00:08:45,817
<i>That was...</i>

99
00:08:52,616 --> 00:08:57,037
Let's finish this.
I'm going to find Night.

100
00:09:01,208 --> 00:09:05,796
Kastehelmi, run! Hurry! Get downstairs!

101
00:09:07,339 --> 00:09:10,591
Lady Kastehelmi,
leave this to me and get inside!

102
00:09:10,592 --> 00:09:11,885
Johann...

103
00:09:12,970 --> 00:09:16,097
This is the Country of Long Nights.

104
00:09:16,098 --> 00:09:17,641
I have to do something!

105
00:09:18,475 --> 00:09:23,063
Spirits of every fireplace and hearth
across the land, heed my call!

106
00:09:28,568 --> 00:09:30,945
You may be small,

107
00:09:30,946 --> 00:09:33,365
but together, you are strong.

108
00:09:34,574 --> 00:09:39,203
Lend me your strength!
I'm second in line to be queen!

109
00:09:39,204 --> 00:09:40,372
My name is Kastehelmi!

110
00:09:47,129 --> 00:09:49,756
Fire? What's happening?

111
00:09:50,716 --> 00:09:53,801
The fireplace and hearth spirits
came to help us.

112
00:09:53,802 --> 00:09:54,928
But...

113
00:09:56,555 --> 00:10:00,808
What's happened to you?
You're usually much smaller.

114
00:10:00,809 --> 00:10:03,769
What? We're just overflowing with power!

115
00:10:03,770 --> 00:10:08,150
The blessing of fire has returned to
this land for the first time in 20 years.

116
00:10:16,408 --> 00:10:18,784
I've served here for years,

117
00:10:18,785 --> 00:10:21,204
but I've never seen anything like this.

118
00:10:21,830 --> 00:10:23,622
Why is this happening all of a sudden?

119
00:10:23,623 --> 00:10:25,292
Why?

120
00:10:25,876 --> 00:10:28,502
You're the one who brought them here.

121
00:10:28,503 --> 00:10:32,007
Those traces of the powers
of fire, ice, and steel.

122
00:10:34,843 --> 00:10:37,511
That red country is guarded by beasts,

123
00:10:37,512 --> 00:10:39,890
so I can't slip inside.

124
00:10:40,807 --> 00:10:43,893
I heard the powers were being split up.

125
00:10:43,894 --> 00:10:45,686
That's the whole reason I came here.

126
00:10:45,687 --> 00:10:49,148
<i>What the hell is this guy talking about?</i>

127
00:10:49,149 --> 00:10:51,068
Is something wrong, Eleonora?

128
00:10:51,651 --> 00:10:56,155
I thought that if this country
refused to let Insomniac go,

129
00:10:56,156 --> 00:10:59,116
you'd be the first one I'd have to fight.

130
00:10:59,117 --> 00:11:02,953
I see. So that's why you asked me that.

131
00:11:02,954 --> 00:11:05,332
Who is the strongest warrior
in this country?

132
00:11:05,916 --> 00:11:09,293
Lady Eleonora, our country would never...

133
00:11:09,294 --> 00:11:13,714
Sorry. I'm not worried
about that anymore. But...

134
00:11:13,715 --> 00:11:16,802
<i>I did ask around about you.</i>

135
00:11:17,511 --> 00:11:20,263
You're a soldier through and through,
and you head the military.

136
00:11:20,889 --> 00:11:23,933
<i>You're also the future prince consort.</i>

137
00:11:23,934 --> 00:11:27,853
You've got all those titles,
and you're close with our diplomat.

138
00:11:27,854 --> 00:11:31,066
There's no way you stay out of politics.

139
00:11:32,234 --> 00:11:34,027
So I have a proposition for you.

140
00:11:35,821 --> 00:11:39,907
Oh, come on.
You can't even handle a little fire?

141
00:11:39,908 --> 00:11:42,077
It's time we settled this.

142
00:11:45,414 --> 00:11:47,040
Shields to the front!

143
00:11:51,545 --> 00:11:53,337
Please, hold it back!

144
00:11:53,338 --> 00:11:54,547
Don't worry.

145
00:11:54,548 --> 00:11:56,632
We have the advantage against ice.

146
00:11:56,633 --> 00:12:00,512
Thank you, Lady Kastehelmi.
I'll find Insomniac.

147
00:12:23,368 --> 00:12:24,743
Well...

148
00:12:24,744 --> 00:12:26,621
We can block it, but...

149
00:12:29,207 --> 00:12:31,042
There's no end to the attack.

150
00:12:31,710 --> 00:12:34,129
So we're at a disadvantage
if this drags on...

151
00:12:37,215 --> 00:12:39,050
<i>What are you doing, Insomniac?</i>

152
00:12:41,011 --> 00:12:46,391
Hungry's back from shopping
with the head cook's daughter.

153
00:12:47,726 --> 00:12:50,520
But Beast-Tamer hasn't returned
from taking the animals out.

154
00:12:51,021 --> 00:12:52,564
I wonder if something happened.

155
00:12:53,732 --> 00:12:56,401
Captain, let's make a deal.

156
00:12:57,861 --> 00:13:00,070
If I drive him off,

157
00:13:00,071 --> 00:13:03,950
tell me what we haven't been told
about this diplomatic mission.

158
00:13:07,245 --> 00:13:10,749
If anything happens to you, how will I
explain it to your knight commander?

159
00:13:12,834 --> 00:13:14,793
Take care of Insomniac for me.

160
00:13:14,794 --> 00:13:16,837
I'm counting on you, Ellie.

161
00:13:16,838 --> 00:13:19,466
No, I'll be fine.

162
00:13:20,425 --> 00:13:21,551
Stand back a little.

163
00:13:22,886 --> 00:13:24,012
Lady Eleonora?

164
00:13:43,240 --> 00:13:47,077
<i>Insomniac, your brothers</i>

165
00:13:48,119 --> 00:13:50,872
<i>are stronger than you
give them credit for!</i>

166
00:14:10,559 --> 00:14:14,563
Beat me, and you can take Insomniac.

167
00:14:24,573 --> 00:14:26,366
Nice and simple. I like it.

168
00:14:26,950 --> 00:14:28,243
<i>Then it's a deal.</i>

169
00:14:31,454 --> 00:14:34,915
<i>He isn't that strong up close,
but he's coming right at me?</i>

170
00:14:34,916 --> 00:14:37,210
<i>Fine by me!</i>

171
00:14:45,051 --> 00:14:46,428
<i>This is just a guess, but...</i>

172
00:14:47,262 --> 00:14:49,263
<i>He turned morning into night...</i>

173
00:14:49,264 --> 00:14:52,934
We've also confirmed that
he can control fire, ice, and water.

174
00:14:53,602 --> 00:14:55,478
<i>...and he controls beasts.</i>

175
00:14:56,813 --> 00:15:00,817
<i>He can probably put me to sleep too.</i>

176
00:15:01,985 --> 00:15:03,987
<i>Is he waiting for the right moment?</i>

177
00:15:05,488 --> 00:15:06,740
<i>Not a chance!</i>

178
00:15:14,539 --> 00:15:16,166
I see.

179
00:15:16,750 --> 00:15:21,754
Did you destroy the Country of Cold
20 years ago...

180
00:15:21,755 --> 00:15:26,426
and gain immense power?
Are you the black-haired Baribara?

181
00:15:27,218 --> 00:15:28,511
<i>Lady Baribara?</i>

182
00:15:29,012 --> 00:15:31,096
<i>She destroyed the Country of Cold?</i>

183
00:15:31,097 --> 00:15:32,932
<i>I've never heard anything about that.</i>

184
00:15:33,433 --> 00:15:35,935
Are you here to destroy this country next?

185
00:15:36,519 --> 00:15:38,479
And what if I am?

186
00:15:38,480 --> 00:15:39,898
What's it to you?

187
00:15:40,523 --> 00:15:42,608
It doesn't matter to me.

188
00:15:42,609 --> 00:15:46,154
But everyone says you're to blame
for my suffering.

189
00:15:47,280 --> 00:15:52,619
So I'll take back the powers you stole,
one by one, and set myself free.

190
00:15:54,621 --> 00:15:55,580
Sorry.

191
00:15:56,206 --> 00:15:58,083
I'm not Baribara.

192
00:15:58,667 --> 00:16:00,752
Really? You're not?

193
00:16:01,419 --> 00:16:03,213
I'm Eleonora.

194
00:16:03,797 --> 00:16:04,798
And you are?

195
00:16:06,091 --> 00:16:07,508
Me?

196
00:16:07,509 --> 00:16:10,178
I'm... Well...

197
00:16:11,721 --> 00:16:13,932
They call me the Visitor.

198
00:16:14,432 --> 00:16:15,892
The Visitor?

199
00:16:18,269 --> 00:16:19,813
This is the first time...

200
00:16:20,397 --> 00:16:22,357
anyone's ever asked my name...

201
00:16:28,279 --> 00:16:31,908
<i>Suddenly, the church bells began to ring.</i>

202
00:16:32,617 --> 00:16:34,077
Could it be...?

203
00:16:35,078 --> 00:16:39,165
<i>Saint Walpurga,
founder of the Country of Long Nights.</i>

204
00:16:40,333 --> 00:16:42,000
<i>Once each year,</i>

205
00:16:42,001 --> 00:16:46,463
<i>she visited this land.
That time had now come.</i>

206
00:16:46,464 --> 00:16:49,759
I can sense a holy presence.

207
00:16:51,052 --> 00:16:54,221
With the Eve beginning so mysteriously,

208
00:16:54,222 --> 00:16:57,016
she must be quite bewildered.

209
00:16:57,851 --> 00:17:01,855
Your Grace, the carriage is ready
to take us to welcome her.

210
00:17:02,564 --> 00:17:03,857
Let us hurry.

211
00:17:04,399 --> 00:17:08,903
No matter what happens, the Spring
Festival must proceed without a hitch.

212
00:17:09,571 --> 00:17:13,073
You two, cross over to the opposite
building via the ground floor

213
00:17:13,074 --> 00:17:14,992
and support Lady Eleonora.

214
00:17:14,993 --> 00:17:15,951
Yes, sir!

215
00:17:15,952 --> 00:17:17,828
You, go to Sir Johann.

216
00:17:17,829 --> 00:17:18,663
Yes, sir.

217
00:17:19,247 --> 00:17:23,334
Lieutenant, take a few men outside
the castle walls. Keep a low profile.

218
00:17:23,835 --> 00:17:26,129
- Guard the archbishop.
- Yes, sir!

219
00:17:26,713 --> 00:17:29,381
Lady Kastehelmi, what's that bell?

220
00:17:29,382 --> 00:17:31,468
Lady Walpurga has arrived.

221
00:17:32,051 --> 00:17:35,554
Saint Walpurga returns on Walpurgis Eve,

222
00:17:35,555 --> 00:17:36,431
isn't that right?

223
00:17:37,015 --> 00:17:38,056
Yes.

224
00:17:38,057 --> 00:17:43,228
He said he'd take your knight commander
to Lady Walpurga.

225
00:17:43,229 --> 00:17:46,065
We can't hand him over now.

226
00:17:47,984 --> 00:17:50,194
Looks like it's time.

227
00:17:50,195 --> 00:17:52,113
I'll be taking Night with me.

228
00:18:12,091 --> 00:18:15,011
So now the bastard's attacking
from a distance!

229
00:18:15,720 --> 00:18:18,972
Lady Kastehelmi, it isn't safe here.

230
00:18:18,973 --> 00:18:21,725
Leave the rest to us
and return to the great hall.

231
00:18:21,726 --> 00:18:24,312
But I want to help look for him!

232
00:18:24,896 --> 00:18:28,482
You should go back. No, please go back.

233
00:18:28,483 --> 00:18:29,984
But, Johann...

234
00:18:30,860 --> 00:18:33,530
You're important to this country.

235
00:18:34,030 --> 00:18:36,074
I can't let you face any more danger.

236
00:18:39,536 --> 00:18:40,954
All right.

237
00:18:44,165 --> 00:18:45,250
<i>Insomniac...</i>

238
00:18:46,584 --> 00:18:48,962
<i>I don't know how you felt...</i>

239
00:18:51,798 --> 00:18:54,633
Johannes, you're a man, aren't you?

240
00:18:54,634 --> 00:18:58,137
Don't you care for drink,
women, or gambling?

241
00:18:58,638 --> 00:19:00,890
<i>They never taught me
about such things at church.</i>

242
00:19:01,891 --> 00:19:04,476
<i>I've always been rather straitlaced,</i>

243
00:19:04,477 --> 00:19:07,522
<i>and my father and brothers
often teased me for it.</i>

244
00:19:08,898 --> 00:19:13,528
Insomniac, do you want our master
to teach you those foolish games too?

245
00:19:14,654 --> 00:19:17,489
Johann, I'd rather learn

246
00:19:17,490 --> 00:19:19,825
to read more difficult books

247
00:19:19,826 --> 00:19:22,328
and learn to write neatly.

248
00:19:25,874 --> 00:19:29,460
<i>When I was sent to the distant capital
to train as a knight,</i>

249
00:19:30,003 --> 00:19:32,463
<i>being beside a model student like you</i>

250
00:19:33,047 --> 00:19:35,008
<i>made me feel right at home.</i>

251
00:19:36,926 --> 00:19:38,636
Hey, Insomniac!

252
00:19:39,679 --> 00:19:41,973
I kept quiet because I was sure
you'd come home,

253
00:19:42,682 --> 00:19:44,433
but if you don't,

254
00:19:44,434 --> 00:19:47,312
Eleonora is going to marry
the chancellor's nephew!

255
00:19:55,486 --> 00:19:56,862
Damn it.

256
00:19:56,863 --> 00:20:00,616
<i>I just can't stand this guy.</i>

257
00:20:00,617 --> 00:20:02,284
<i>He gets on my nerves.</i>

258
00:20:02,285 --> 00:20:03,620
<i>And now I know why.</i>

259
00:20:04,746 --> 00:20:09,042
<i>He keeps talking about Insomniac
like he owns him.</i>

260
00:20:16,049 --> 00:20:18,551
<i>I can't let up now...</i>

261
00:20:21,804 --> 00:20:24,015
You're getting sloppy!

262
00:20:25,558 --> 00:20:27,018
<i>Insomniac...</i>

263
00:20:28,895 --> 00:20:30,480
<i>I'll never...</i>

264
00:20:33,942 --> 00:20:37,570
let you take him!

265
00:20:42,116 --> 00:20:43,116
I'll knock you down.

266
00:20:43,117 --> 00:20:45,995
You're the one who's going to fall.

267
00:20:46,579 --> 00:20:47,956
Eleonora.

268
00:20:50,083 --> 00:20:55,254
<i>Damn it. He had another trick
up his sleeve?</i>

269
00:21:01,844 --> 00:21:05,514
That light has no place in my domain.

270
00:21:05,515 --> 00:21:06,641
Night...!

271
00:21:07,225 --> 00:21:08,768
- I...
- You...

272
00:21:10,019 --> 00:21:11,270
are out of time.

273
00:21:15,149 --> 00:21:17,568
You'd better leave
before you vanish completely.

274
00:21:18,361 --> 00:21:21,363
But I was going to beat Eleonora...

275
00:21:21,364 --> 00:21:22,240
She's...

276
00:21:22,865 --> 00:21:24,909
strong even in the dark.

277
00:21:26,035 --> 00:21:29,746
If anyone says anything,
tell them I did it.

278
00:21:29,747 --> 00:21:32,667
I'm used to getting scolded by Nanny.

279
00:21:34,085 --> 00:21:39,799
I, Night, have belonged to her
for a long time.

280
00:21:41,342 --> 00:21:43,720
You can't win.

281
00:21:47,682 --> 00:21:50,435
You belong to her...?

282
00:21:53,771 --> 00:21:55,106
I'll be back.

283
00:22:13,458 --> 00:22:14,876
What's with that guy...?

284
00:22:15,877 --> 00:22:18,171
He backed off so easily.

285
00:22:20,465 --> 00:22:21,507
We haven't...

286
00:22:22,008 --> 00:22:23,259
settled this yet...

287
00:22:30,141 --> 00:22:32,727
Why did he know your name?

288
00:22:33,394 --> 00:22:36,897
What? Who cares about that
at a time like this?

289
00:22:36,898 --> 00:22:38,940
- More importantly...
- It might

290
00:22:38,941 --> 00:22:40,651
not matter to you,

291
00:22:41,277 --> 00:22:43,863
but there are some things
I just can't bear!

292
00:22:46,199 --> 00:22:49,118
Always... In all the years to come...

293
00:22:50,828 --> 00:22:51,996
Forever...

294
00:23:05,093 --> 00:23:05,968
Honestly...

295
00:23:09,514 --> 00:23:14,268
I still have no idea
what you're talking about.

296
00:24:47,153 --> 00:24:52,200
<i>Something must've happened to the Night,
to Marronnier's knight commander.</i>

297
00:24:52,825 --> 00:24:55,453
{\an8}<i>I'll go about things
much better than he did!</i>

298
00:24:58,539 --> 00:25:00,958
WHEN NIGHT ENDS

